<section id="credentials">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">The Diagnostic Capability Across Three Disciplines</div>
    <h2>What no single specialist can offer.</h2>
    <p style="color:var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size:0.9rem;">
      A UX designer diagnoses at the interface layer. A growth consultant diagnoses at the
      funnel layer. Neither has the structural vocabulary to diagnose at the architecture layer —
      where information sequencing, domain contracts, and cognitive scaffolding determine whether
      users activate or leave. That diagnosis requires all three disciplines simultaneously.
    </p>

    <div class="cred-grid">
      <div class="cred-card">
        <div class="cred-institution">UNAM · B.A. Literature · 2015</div>
        <div class="cred-degree">Structural Analysis — Reading What Systems Don't Say</div>
        <div class="cred-detail">
          Most friction audits stop at the event log — they record where users leave,
          not why the architecture made leaving easier than continuing. Formal training
          in structural analysis: identifying hidden assumptions, unstated constraints,
          and breaks in internal logic that automated instrumentation cannot surface.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cred-card">
        <div class="cred-institution">UNAM · M.A. Pedagogy · 2020</div>
        <div class="cred-degree">Cognitive Scaffolding — How Users Build Understanding Under Uncertainty</div>
        <div class="cred-detail">
          Your onboarding flow was designed by engineers who understand your product —
          not by people who understand how users construct mental models when the product
          is new to them. This is the scientific basis for that construction: how information
          must be sequenced to build understanding rather than create cognitive debt.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cred-card">
        <div class="cred-institution">UdeG · B.Sc. Web Systems Dev. · 2025 · GPA 98.5</div>
        <div class="cred-degree">Systems Engineering — Diagnose to the Code Level</div>
        <div class="cred-detail">
          Most onboarding consultants diagnose without being able to specify what needs
          to change at the architecture level. The technical grounding here produces
          findings specific enough for an engineering team to act on — not a UX recommendation,
          a structural diagnosis with a decision record.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cred-card">
        <div class="cred-institution">2011 → 2026</div>
        <div class="cred-degree">The Longitudinal Proof — A Live System, Not a Case Study</div>
        <div class="cred-detail">
          huhuGERMAN has served 30–40 real users per trimester since 2011. The friction event
          documented in 2024 — AI behavior governed by implicit assumptions about user state —
          and the typed domain contract that resolved it, are running in production. This is
          not a framework in a PDF. It is a system you can inspect.
          <a href="/predictive-analysis" style="color: var(--orange-light);">Full analysis →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
